{"abstract":"Using action research methodology, this research applies sustainability design principles in developing digital sustainability designs for a public procurement agency. The practical results indicate a design for continuous process of sustainability goal setting activities, “greening” rather than “green.” This process results in an organization that is continuously resetting its green objectives; never fully satisfied by its green achievements, it is always seeking to adopt the next green goals on the horizon. These results are an extension of the use of continuous quality improvement in managing green and sustainable information systems. Nevertheless, a greening organizational process provides material evidence for satisfying EU sustainability criteria while placing the organization in a state of perpetual green leadership.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Baskerville, Richard","Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-820845"],"event":{"end":"2025-01-10","place":"Honolulu, us","start":"2025-01-07","title":"58th Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences, HICSS 2025","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University"],"keyword":["Action research","Design principles","Digital sustainability","Green IS","Green IT"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sustainability design principles the greening of an organization","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.24251/hicss.2025.702","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-820845","identifier":[{"id":"105005154756","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-93a0a100-4a68-4378-bd6b-26eb53ce81f3"],"keyword":["Action Research","Design Principles","Digital Sustainability","Green IS","Green IT"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-943EBA8CD0EC0F655839E0B35D6A5F9B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.24251/hicss.2025.702","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/111930113/0573.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Sustainable Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Richard","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tung X.","key":"buipedh","last":"Bui","name":"Bui, Tung X.","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.24251/hicss.2025.702","eisbn":["9780998133188"],"issn":["15301605"],"pages":"5860-5869","publisher":"IEEE Computer Society Press","series":"Proceedings of the Annual Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Annual Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences"},"review":"Peer Review