},{"affno":"2","first":"Kasper","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"558df261-ca9f-440a-8bee-7d38813c253f","name":"Iversen, Kasper","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter","key":"garredpau","last":"Garred","locid":"854d72a7-c955-43b5-b455-b7ea1f9bcb1e","name":"Garred, Peter","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Susanne Dam","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2baa36fa-2709-482a-9595-52c5b9537801","name":"Nielsen, Susanne Dam","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34841629"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/joim.13419","issn":["09546820","09557873"],"issn_org":["09546820"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Internal Medicine","pages":"513-518","status":"p","title":"Journal of Internal Medicine","volume":"291"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121385903"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-20879e9c-7967-4c3f-8090-38e3326115e5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Humoral response to two doses of BNT162b2 vaccination in people with HIV","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-412818","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"As the gravity of the impact of climate change on everyday life grows ever more relevant, green technology involving sustainability are also garnering more attention, and, in turn, more sophisticated IT solutions are needed. In this paper we review existing literature on the diffusion and transfer of technology in households in order to strengthen and prepare the future adoption of more IT-oriented sustainability solutions of green IT. We find that a large portion of household studies have taken place in the farming and agricultural sector of developing countries. We find that a large portion of the studies propose implications from a government policy perspective. We also find that a large portion of studies confirm factors influencing the diffusion and adoption coming from diffusion theory. Another significant portion takes a socio-cultural approach perspective. Finally, we find that collaboration, co-creation and participation seem to be effective in furthering the transfer and diffusion of sustainable and green technology in households. We discuss the implications of these different approaches when tackling the diffusion of green IT and propose taking a pluralist and design-oriented perspective since no single perspective or approach so far has resulted in large-scale technology transfer or diffusion to households.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt","Christensen, Jeffrey Andrew"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-561864"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-16","place":"Kildare, ie","start":"2022-06-15","title":"IFIP 8.6 - Technology Adoption Group","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adoption","Co creation","Diffusion","Green IT","Households","Participatory","Policy","Socio cultural","Technology transfer"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reviewing transfer and diffusion of climate technology in households towards a greener it future","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-561864","identifier":[{"id":"85140774271","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-583033e5-76c4-4ffa-a066-1283563fa6d8"],"keyword":["Adoption","Climate technologies","Co-creation","Diffusion","Green IT","Households","Participatory","Policy","Socio-cultural","Technology transfer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-20CB8757AF5D4AF7AA7DF56722DB5154"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Sustainable Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Magnus Rotvit Perlt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d9c2134a-0799-45eb-8a15-e0523fc96da2","name":"Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jeffrey Andrew","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"7ad9822d-5c18-4ce3-9fa0-6b36ab30e445","name":"Christensen, Jeffrey Andrew","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Amany","key":"elbannapedh","last":"Elbanna","name":"Elbanna, Amany","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Shane","key":"mcloughlinpedh","last":"Mcloughlin","name":"Mcloughlin, Shane","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Yogesh K.","key":"dwivedipedh","last":"Dwivedi","name":"Dwivedi, Yogesh K.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Brian","key":"donnellanpedh","last":"Donnellan","name":"Donnellan, Brian","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"wastellpedh","last":"Wastell","name":"Wastell, David","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-17968-6_13","isbn":["9783031179679"],"issn":["18684238"],"pages":"163-176","publisher":"Springer","series":"IFIP AICT - Advances in Information and Communication technology","status":"p","subtitle":"IFIP WG 8.6 International Working Conference on Transfer and Diffusion of IT, TDIT 2022, Maynooth, Ireland, June 15–16, 2022, Proceedings","title":"Co-creating for Context in the Transfer and Diffusion of IT"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140774271"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-583033e5-76c4-4ffa-a066-1283563fa6d8"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Reviewing Transfer and Diffusion of Climate Technology in Households : Towards a Greener IT Future","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-561864","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"This paper first explains how IT project management became a profession by first being included in project management in general through organizations such as PMI and IPMA and later by developing as a scientific community within AIS in its own right. Second, the paper describes how agility and the agile methods developed and took over much of the IT project arena. However, IT project management had to respond to the â€œbig waveâ€� of agile, and we explain how they did that through the professional communities IPMA and PMI that developed agile versions of their recommendations and certifications. In parallel with this development, agile was professionalized in its own right by organizations such as the Agile Alliance and scrum.org. We conclude by discussing whether agile and the organizations trying to make it into a profession have achieved enough autonomy to professionalize agile.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Baskervillle, Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-564294"],"event":{"end":"2022-03-19","place":"Myrtle Beach, us","start":"2022-03-18","title":"24th annual Meeting of the Southern Association for Information Systems","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University"],"keyword":["Agile","Autonomy","Professionalization","Project management"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how agile it project management was professionalized","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/sais2022/19","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-564294","ids":["ruc-7bd2464e-e814-4a7d-b0ab-49a2ee5179da"],"keyword":["Agile","Autonomy","Professionalization","Project Management"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-24C43E906360499FAE4CD6634A5518F1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/sais2022/19","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Richard","key":"baskervilllepau","last":"Baskervillle","name":"Baskervillle, Richard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"AIS Association","status":"p","title":"SAIS 2022 Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-7bd2464e-e814-4a7d-b0ab-49a2ee5179da"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"How agile IT project management was professionalized","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-564294","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"IS (Information Systems) Project Managers need to navigate complexity in many ways. This navigation is inherently difficult because it is an experientially learned process with many externally changing elements, meaning that it takes experience, theory, reflection, and active experimentation to become good at navigating the complexity that IS projects impose. This is an important challenge to tackle for institutions that want to educate potential candidates for IS project management. How can we possibly include both practice and theory and develop IS practitioners’ skills and level of reflection when it comes to navigating complexity? We took on this challenge as teachers of IS project management because of its complex nature and used IS project management for designing a serious game to make the intangible tangible; by translating the understanding of complexity into prescriptive logics to identify a suitable and effective learning mechanism. Our design science research approach was that of “building and learning” and we report on the difficulties of translation between theory, practical context, and target audience, finding a balance between ‘fun’ and ‘learning’, as well as the impact on group dynamics and applicability of rationalizing rigorous approaches to navigating complexity. We tested the designed board game on both regular students, executive master students, and even realworld practitioners. The game let the participants engage various situations in which they must find a solution based on a theory-informed heuristic reasoning process and a facilitated feedback process.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt","Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-557344"],"event":{"end":"2022-08-17","place":"Helsinge, dk","start":"2022-08-14","title":"13th Scandinavian Conference on Information Systems 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design science research","Education","Serious games","Teaching"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"training is project managers to deal with complexity a design science research approach using serious gaming","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/83493360/20220620_IRIS2022_paper_DesigningISProjectManagementComplexityGames.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-557344","ids":["ruc-142a27b5-af64-483d-bc42-ebbd237335ce"],"keyword":["Design Science Research","Education","IS Project Management","Serious Games","Teaching"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-309F34791D25A2B14D9BB126543FF6C3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/83493360/20220620_IRIS2022_paper_DesigningISProjectManagementComplexityGames.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Magnus Rotvit Perlt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d9c2134a-0799-45eb-8a15-e0523fc96da2","name":"Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-142a27b5-af64-483d-bc42-ebbd237335ce"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Training Is Project Managers To Deal With Complexity : A Design Science Research Approach Using Serious Gaming","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-557344","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-557530"],"event":{"end":"2022-12-11","place":"København, dk","start":"2022-12-11","title":"SIGGreen Pre-ICIS 2022 Workshop","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital nudging loop","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-557530","ids":["ruc-16eefe29-4652-4baa-94b5-cb73c0116664"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A0D0C8FC37AECDE7623D8DA236119D3C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Magnus Rotvit Perlt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d9c2134a-0799-45eb-8a15-e0523fc96da2","name":"Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-16eefe29-4652-4baa-94b5-cb73c0116664"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Digital nudging loop","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-557530","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"IS designers lack necessary research skills to develop evidence for IS designs. They are trained in development methods, researching user requirements, functional requirements, and non-functional requirements. But many, if not most, lack training in how to research the published scientific evidence that could inform their designs. Such published evidence will often span across broader issues for consideration in IS designs. For example, if a designer wishes to consider the social implications of their application of artificial intelligence (AI) in an IS design, they might take an evidence-based approach to such a design. This paper describes how current evidence-based practices apply to evidence-based information systems design, and how such an approach informs information systems designers about scientific evidence concerning problem- and solution-oriented knowledge, human and social values, ethics, impacts, and implications. By better informing professional information systems designers, evidence-based information systems design provides strong grounding for the inclusion of values and ethics in future information systems.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Baskervillle, Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-562303"],"event":{"end":"2022-12-10","place":"København, dk","start":"2022-12-10","title":"Pre-ICIS OASIS Workshop 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evidence based information systems design how research can inform sociotechnical ai design","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-562303","ids":["ruc-5eeef523-a5a7-4e8b-ac6a-bf277caaba07"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-062F201569D67D6D58EEE109E114E7A8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Richard","key":"baskervilllepau","last":"Baskervillle","name":"Baskervillle, Richard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-5eeef523-a5a7-4e8b-ac6a-bf277caaba07"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Evidence-based Information Systems Design : How Research Can Inform Sociotechnical AI Design","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-562303","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of this paper is to demonstrate how digital organizational resilience was a key to digital transformation success in the public sector of Denmark. Using a historical research method, we analyze the information systems (IS) history from 1998 to 2019 at all three levels of the public sector in Denmark. This study discovers the historical events regarding the barriers and hindrances to digital transformation in Denmark and shows how resilience enabled continuity in the transformation. Using significant events in the history of Denmark becoming a digitalized nation, we find a pattern of what constitutes digital organizational resilience in e-government: first, there are new ways to strategize digitalization, second, there is a collaborative strategy in execution across the public sector that envelopes the ability to learn from overcoming barriers and hindrances, and third, there is an organizational resilience path that iterates action, collaboration, and learning. Digital resilience has previously been studied in the context of individual learning and cyber security. The pattern found in the historical account is a promising basis for understanding and achieving resilience in a transformative digitalization strategy in the public sector.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Fleron, Benedicte","Pries-Heje, Jan","Baskerville, Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-557043"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University"],"keyword":["Digital Organizational Resilience","E government","IS History","Policies and Strategies for Digital Government","Strategy"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"becoming a most digitalized country a history of digital organizational resilience in denmark","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-557043","identifier":[{"id":"85137140941","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-0fc78c47-edab-413b-ba0f-5fed680be606"],"keyword":["Digital Organizational Resilience","E-government","IS History","Policies and Strategies for Digital Government","Strategy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-CEEA6674A92987B0A467AFC684C6C3D7"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Benedicte","key":"fleronpau","last":"Fleron","locid":"1eac1461-da4c-47d8-9661-106a1a39ae9f","name":"Fleron, Benedicte","orcid":"0009-0002-6000-9923","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Richard","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.17705/1cais.05107","issn":["15293181"],"issue":"1","journal":"Communications of the Association for Information Systems","pages":"120-139","paperid":"16","status":"p","title":"Communications of the Association for Information Systems","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137140941"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-0fc78c47-edab-413b-ba0f-5fed680be606"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Becoming a most Digitalized Country : A History of Digital Organizational Resilience in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-557043","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Existing research reveals an overlap between the capabilities of an agile organization and the capabilities of a resilient organization. Using evidence from longitudinal case studies of three organizations, this paper explains how organizational resilience can be assimilated from organizational agility; and how organizational agility can be assimilated from IT project agility. The cases show how the capability to negotiate known contradictions in both resilience and agility is one facilitating feature in this assimilation.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Baskerville, Richard L."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-565591"],"event":{"acronym":"ICIS","end":"2021-12-15","place":"Austin, us","start":"2021-12-12","title":"International Conference on Information Systems","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"achieving resilience through agility","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/icis2021/is_resilience/is_resilience/8/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-565591","ids":["ruc-8ea09649-f014-4af1-82bc-0c51cb10c379"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1A6A00736960D6AF121DCCD6D577660B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Sustainable Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Richard L.","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard L.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"8","publisher":"ICIS","series":"Proceedings of the International Conference on Information Systems","status":"p","subtitle":"Building Sustainability and Resilience with IS: A Call for Action","title":"ICIS 2021 Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-8ea09649-f014-4af1-82bc-0c51cb10c379"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Achieving Resilience through Agility","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-565591","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of this paper is to demonstrate how digital organizational resilience was a key to digital transformation success in the public sector of Denmark. Using a historical research method, we analyze the IS history from 1998-2019 at all three levels of the public sector in Denmark. This study finds historical events about barriers and hindrances and shows how resilience enabled continuity in the transformation. We find a pattern of three elements in the history of what constitutes digital organizational resilience in e-government: digitalization strategy, collaboration across the public sector, and the ability to learn from overcoming barriers and hindrances. Digital resilience has previously been studied in the context of individual learning and cyber security. This pattern is a promising basis for understanding and achieving resilience in a transformative digitalization strategy in the public sector.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fleron, Benedicte","Pries-Heje, Jan","Baskerville, Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-559640"],"event":{"acronym":"HICSS","end":"2021-01-08","place":"Honolulu, us","start":"2021-01-04","title":"54th Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Curtin University","Georgia State University"],"keyword":["IS History","Policies and Strategies for Digital Government","Strategy","eGovernment"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital organizational resilience a history of denmark as a most digitalized country","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access