","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788778675347"],"pages":"91-112","place":"Roskilde","publisher":"Roskilde Universitetsforlag","status":"p","title":"At the junction of project leadership and innovation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9fb0880a-1e54-4833-8b26-7f7cb867a107"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Tracing the footsteps of reflective practice in project management education","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-220319","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"When an experienced assessor enters a company there are certain characteristic symptoms that reveals the maturity of the company even before the assessment. In this paper we start out from a list of 32 characteristic symptomatic problems generated by two experienced assessors after maturity assessments in more than 300 companies. We then use cognitive mapping asking five times why to get behind the symptomatic problems and reveal the underlying problems or causes of the problems. Our mapping revealed a number of interesting relationships between the symptomatic problems. We then evaluated our findings by building a tool in the form of a website where users could score statements - formulated from the symptoms - and from that we could point them to areas where they probably needed to improve. We improved the tool in three learning cycles of design evaluation and ended up in a summative evaluation where we compared the outcome of using the website tool with a CMMI maturity assessment. We conclude that looking for symptoms, and as an individual scoring statements build on the symptoms, can point to improvement areas. However, doing so is not a replacement for a maturity assessment, the scoring of statements cannot necessarily reveal the maturity of the organization.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Johansen, Jørn","Korsaa, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-566739"],"event":{"end":"2020-09-11","place":"Düsseldorf, de","start":"2020-09-09","title":"27th EuroSPI Conference","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CMMI","Cognitive map","Improvement","Maturity","Process improvement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a cognitive map of maturity symptom based improvement recommendations","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/77820275/Pries_Heje_et_al_2020_A_Cognitive_map_of_Maturity_EuroSPI_2020.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-566739","identifier":[{"id":"85089715630","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-9f6ef615-065a-4594-9590-04a2f0bcd242"],"keyword":["CMMI","Cognitive map","Improvement","Maturity","Process improvement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-87EBC4C4E36D457596602924F32D4C53"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/77820275/Pries_Heje_et_al_2020_A_Cognitive_map_of_Maturity_EuroSPI_2020.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Sustainable Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Whitebox"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jørn","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Jørn","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Morten","key":"korsaapau","last":"Korsaa","name":"Korsaa, Morten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Murat","key":"yilmazpedh","last":"Yilmaz","name":"Yilmaz, Murat","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul","key":"clarkepedh","last":"Clarke","name":"Clarke, Paul","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jörg","key":"niemannpedh","last":"Niemann","name":"Niemann, Jörg","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Richard","key":"messnarzpedh","last":"Messnarz","name":"Messnarz, Richard","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-56441-4_33","eisbn":["9783030564414"],"isbn":["9783030564407"],"pages":"447-461","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"27th European Conference, EuroSPI 2020, Düsseldorf, Germany, September 9–11, 2020, Proceedings","title":"Systems, Software and Services Process Improvement - 27th European Conference, EuroSPI 2020, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089715630"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Roskilde University","Universities","whitebox"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-9f6ef615-065a-4594-9590-04a2f0bcd242"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"A Cognitive map of Maturity : Symptom-based improvement recommendations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-566739","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In this chapter we identify characteristics of a certain type of IT mega project that, when large majority of the public are supposed to be end-users, can run the risk of becoming impervious to the usual project management best practices, despite the fact that best practices seemed to work well in the process of the project. We coin this type of mega projects as \"Volatile Mega IT\" due to their nature of being easy to notice but difficult to grasp. This nature makes it very hard to evaluate the results of VMIT projects because the recipients of the evaluation results are entangled or part of the system and its evaluation results. Through the characteristics we identify a possible new sublime, a construct of major influence on mega projects, that manifests itself as the negative publicity which a stakeholder group enmanates around the IT mega project. In line with the current overall theme of this book we argue that new innovative and practically useful approaches are needed to evaluate IT mega projects that can handle this new sublime in ways that previous methods seem unable.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fleron, Benedicte","Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-569385"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Projektledelse"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mega it as public property a call for innovative evaluation methods","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-569385","ids":["ruc-c7947ae7-2902-4081-9676-2b79aebbccc6"],"keyword":["mega it","projektledelse","sundhedsplatform"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2006F6F716FABEC5B0864F172D1A3F85"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Sustainable Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Benedicte","key":"fleronpau","last":"Fleron","locid":"1eac1461-da4c-47d8-9661-106a1a39ae9f","name":"Fleron, Benedicte","orcid":"0009-0002-6000-9923","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Magnus Rotvit Perlt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d9c2134a-0799-45eb-8a15-e0523fc96da2","name":"Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Magnus R.P.","key":"hansenpedh","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Magnus R.P.","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepedh","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","isbn":["9788778675347"],"pages":"75-90","place":"Roskilde","publisher":"Roskilde Universitetsforlag","status":"p","title":"In the junction of leadership and innovation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-c7947ae7-2902-4081-9676-2b79aebbccc6"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Mega IT as Public Property : A Call for Innovative Evaluation Methods","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-569385","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The research sheds light on how collaborative project Business Model Innovation (BMI) can enable innovation for more energy production with less costs within offshore wind park energy ecosystems. The empirical qualitative research took place from September 2017 to June 2018 in a Baltic Sea port. The findings highlight the essentials of successful collaborative project BMI in the research context. The findings are summarized and illustrated in the model called \"Project FrontEco BMI\". The approach shown in the model created value through higher reliability and faster flow through the port with less investments required. The contribution shed light on the hitherto black box of ecosystem innovation to contain BMI on overall project level enabled by heterogeneous individual and organisational preferred behaviours and horizontal knowledge creation in project execution.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Brink, Tove"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-638152"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Business model innovation BMI","Collaboration","Ecosystems","Innovation","Port development","Projects"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"collaborative project business model innovation for horizontal leadership in projects qualitative empirical research in the offshore wind energy ecosystem","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://samfundslitteratur.dk/bog/junction-project-leadership-and-innovation","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-638152","ids":["sdu-e2b7ccc0-b564-4360-8d17-14c087fd0121"],"keyword":["Business model innovation (BMI)","Collaboration","Ecosystems","Innovation","Port Development","Projects"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8A42C7DA7486ACC91E455F3D79BD5FA1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Sociology, Environmental and Business Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tove","key":"brinkpau","last":"Brink","locid":"4767043a-dec0-4b2b-ae68-4757cbb3b493","name":"Brink, Tove","orcid":"0000-0003-0524-9211","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Magnus R.P.","key":"hansenpedh","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Magnus R.P.","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepedh","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788778675422"],"pages":"11-36","place":"Roskilde","publisher":"Roskilde Universitetsforlag","status":"p","title":"At the junction of project leadership and innovation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e2b7ccc0-b564-4360-8d17-14c087fd0121"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Collaborative project business model innovation for horizontal leadership in projects : Qualitative empirical research in the offshore wind energy ecosystem","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-638152","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This working paper gives an account of a literature review of what we know about changing household behavior with Green IT. It is a review paper meaning that we have been searching and reading the existing literature on behavioral change in relation to IT. And we have been searching the literature on Green IT.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt","Tchatchoua, Nadine Sandjo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-561340"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to change household behaviour with green it review of literature","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/75607731/RUC_Working_Paper_How_to_change_household_behaviour_with_Green_IT.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-561340","ids":["ruc-500ef24c-6709-4e34-9d6c-c38831bd7da9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C7A18F7EB6B299D792EDDF2A988EA481"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/75607731/RUC_Working_Paper_How_to_change_household_behaviour_with_Green_IT.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Sustainable Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key