{"abstract":"The smart city concept is used as tool by local and municipal governments to deliver benefits relating to people, government, economy, mobility, environment and living. By embedding technologies and the internet of things in the city’s infrastructure, smart cities aim to generate insights that drive local im-provements and accrue to a global level. The smart city is also viewed as a transformative lever for government. As cities move beyond smart city pilot showcasing projects, they face the challenge of embedding smart city initiatives in business-as-usual. Despite ambitious goals and high stakes, little is known about the work that leaders perform in undertaking this transformation. This study explored the leadership practice of smart city leaders in Denmark, Holland, USA, Australia and New Zealand. We focus on how leaders drive transformation from showcasing to becoming a sustainable smart city, and the challenges faced. As result we present a framework of six barriers to overcome and five enacted leadership roles to transform the city of today to a future sustainable smart city. We use institutional logics as a lens to discuss and explain the challenges faced by city leaders and their critical role as innovation agents and boundary spanners in smart city transformation.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Cranefield, Jocelyn","Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-569355"],"event":{"acronym":"ECIS","end":"2019-06-14","place":"Stockholm, se","start":"2019-06-08","title":"27th European Conference on Information Systems","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["New Zealand"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Victoria University of Wellington"],"keyword":["Institutional logics","Leadership","Smart City","Sustainability","Transformation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"moving beyond showcasing the five faces of leadership in smart city transformation","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/ecis2019_rp/113/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-569355","identifier":[{"id":"85087108305","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-c73bd7e9-f760-45bd-8085-32eafd232fbd"],"keyword":["Institutional logics","Leadership","Smart city","Transformation","sustainability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-049B72240554B6A35A3CAD280809BC1A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/ecis2019_rp/113/","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nz","key":"victoria university of wellington","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Victoria University of Wellington","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Sustainable Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jocelyn","key":"cranefieldpau","last":"Cranefield","name":"Cranefield, Jocelyn","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"vombrockepedh","last":"vom Brocke","name":"vom Brocke, Jan","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Shirley","key":"gregorpedh","last":"Gregor","name":"Gregor, Shirley","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Oliver","key":"mullerpedh","last":"Muller","name":"Muller, Oliver","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781733632508"],"isbn":["9781733632508"],"issn":["00000034"],"publisher":"AIS Association","series":"Proceedings of the European Conference on Information Systems","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 27th European Conference on Information Systems (ECIS), Stockholm &amp; Uppsala, Sweden, June 8-14, 2019","volume":"2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087108305"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-c73bd7e9-f760-45bd-8085-32eafd232fbd"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Moving beyond showcasing : The five faces of leadership in smart city transformation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-569355","year":"2019","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Design science research aims to be prescriptive, purposeful, relevant, and valuable. The propagation of design science theory, models, and principles is a key challenge. In this paper, we discuss this propagation issue and propose an alternative to the backward-looking concept of generalization; namely, the concept of projectability. We present projectability as providing a language for explaining how design theories and design principles, as prescriptive constructs, imply intentionality for operation in other places or times. In 2008, a special issue of MISQ published five design science exemplars. We analyzed the actual projection of the design theories and principles from these papers and found several notable actual projections for all five. However, in all but one case, the papers that developed the projections involved one or more of the original authors. This paucity of propagation indicates that DSR publications need better framing to enable their projectability. Hence, we propose a language and a projection process logic in six parts that better frame (and improve) such projectability.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Baskerville, Richard","Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-558957"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"projectability in design science research","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/jitta/vol20/iss1/3/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-558957","ids":["ruc-2cab7c87-cd75-405c-a76d-3f36ceec50bb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AAB17B65F3A5F811D187DA744729E169"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Sustainable Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Richard","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["15324516"],"issn_org":["15526496"],"issue":"1","journal":"JITTA","status":"p","title":"JITTA","title_org":"JITTA: Journal of Information Technology Theory & Application","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-2cab7c87-cd75-405c-a76d-3f36ceec50bb"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Projectability in Design Science Research","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-558957","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
