{"abstract":"The importance of creativity is widely acknowledged in design science research, yet there is a lack of understanding of how this creativity is manifested throughout the design science lifecycle. This research examines the effects of the boundaries that are placed on creativity by the particular design science research method used throughout the design cycles and iterations. The progressive and methodical nature of design science research imposes structure comprising rational and creative, boundaries on the problem-solving process. These boundaries determine when and where to iterate to a specific previous stage. A set of iteration indicators, derived from the literature on creativity and bounded rationality, provide the design researcher with guidance on how to recognize that the time for iteration is nigh. These indicators are evaluated using a case study for the design of creative, pervasive games.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Baskerville, Richard","Storey, Veda C.","Kaul, Mala"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-565691"],"event":{"acronym":"DESRIST","end":"2019-06-06","place":"Worchester MA, us","start":"2019-06-04","title":"14th International Conference on Design Science Research in Information Systems and Technology","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University","University of Nevada, Reno"],"keyword":["Bounded creativity","Bounded rationality","Creativity","Design science research","Designing","Rigor","Site storming","Theorizing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inducing creativity in design science research","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/75272927/InducingCreativityInDSR_final_to_DESRIST.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-565691","identifier":[{"id":"85066028535","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-901ef9b7-f1e7-42b7-8701-304cf0ce8e4d"],"keyword":["Bounded creativity","Bounded rationality","Creativity","Design science research","Designing","Iteration indicators","Rigor","Site-storming","Theorizing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FB2586EB6DBD7CC41AF364CB26AF0B2F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/75272927/InducingCreativityInDSR_final_to_DESRIST.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Sustainable Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of nevada reno","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Nevada, Reno","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Richard","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Veda C.","key":"storeypau","last":"Storey","name":"Storey, Veda C.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Mala","key":"kaulpau","last":"Kaul","name":"Kaul, Mala","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gondy","key":"leroypedh","last":"Leroy","name":"Leroy, Gondy","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bengisu","key":"tulupedh","last":"Tulu","name":"Tulu, Bengisu","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Soussan","key":"djamasbipedh","last":"Djamasbi","name":"Djamasbi, Soussan","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-19504-5_1","eisbn":["9783030195045"],"isbn":["9783030195038"],"pages":"3-17","publisher":"Springer","series":"Proceedings of the International Conference on Design Science Research in Information Systems and Technology","status":"p","subtitle":"14th International Conference on Design Science Research in Information Systems and Technology, DESRIST 2019, Worcester, MA, USA, June 4–6, 2019, Proceedings","title":"Extending the Boundaries of Design Science Theory and Practice"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066028535"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-901ef9b7-f1e7-42b7-8701-304cf0ce8e4d"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Inducing Creativity in Design Science Research","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-565691","year":"2019","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"End-user redesign has been coined as a phenomenon that may happen within IT platforms such as Facebook or Wikipedia. However, redesign or secondary design outside the boundaries of a platform is under-researched. Existing prescriptive knowledge is limited to designing functionality of an artefact with specific boundaries where redesign can take place, not on why and how to enable novel unbounded redesign outside the original scope that can benefit decision making and organisation. Hence, we need design theories that can help primary designers create artefacts that allow unbounded secondary (re-)design. We propose design principles for this unbounded secondary design. The principles are derived from a group decision support tool case that was presented, redesigned and infused into two different organisational domains. Thus, the contribution of the paper is a design theory in the form of two times three design principles aimed at supporting the secondary design process and theform and function of the secondary design.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt","Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-556216"],"event":{"acronym":"ECIS","end":"2018-06-28","place":"Portsmouth, gb","start":"2018-06-23","title":"26th European Conference on Information Systems","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design principles","Diffusion","FORM","Function","Implementation","Infusion","Secondary design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"principles for unbounded secondary design","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/ecis2018_rp/133/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-556216","identifier":[{"id":"85061330968","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-0300195b-5afa-4bb0-9ad6-373d8a8ece1f"],"keyword":["Design Principles","Diffusion","Form","Function","Implementation","Infusion","Secondary Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-397888FD5BD330160CE8F01E15B67AE6"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Magnus Rotvit Perlt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d9c2134a-0799-45eb-8a15-e0523fc96da2","name":"Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00000034"],"journal":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems","paperid":"133","status":"p","title":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems","title_org":"Proceedings of the European Conference on Information Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-0300195b-5afa-4bb0-9ad6-373d8a8ece1f"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Principles for Unbounded Secondary design","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-556216","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"I dette kapitel fokuserer vi på kompleksitet i projekter. Kompleksitet er et emne, der er blevet mere og mere aktuelt, så til årets projektlederundersøgelse mente vi, at det var uomgængeligt at tage med. Relevansen af emnet illustreres også tydeligt af, at det er årets ”højdespringer”, hvad angår de udfordringer, som projektlederne oplever. Konkret er det gået fra en 8. plads til en 2. plads.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Mikkelsen, Mogens Frank"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-557138"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kompleksitet i projekter","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dra","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.mannaz.com/da/konsulentydelser/program-og-projektledelse/projektlederundersoegelsen-2018/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-557138","ids":["ruc-1127a6a7-383d-4d53-a6b8-b412480754f2"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-69CD8B64FB0AF9FE817CBE46B90D0C02"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.mannaz.com/da/konsulentydelser/program-og-projektledelse/projektlederundersoegelsen-2018/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","coun