rsities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Other Companies","Private Research","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen","whitebox","whitebox aps (biz)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1c93f8e0-2462-47ee-afd3-66fc40a813d8","ruc-b0a40cd0-deb9-492a-8f18-cd529f28aa9d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Improving the Choice of Organizational Change Strategy","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.06-756219","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"A Smart City takes advantage of new technologies; Internet-of-Things; Machine Learning and Artificial Intelligence; Data Analytics; Robots; just to mention some. But being smart in 2018 is also about sustainability. Becoming a Sustainable Smart City (SSC) is all about Organizational Change. That requires leadership, timely decision making, and effective execution of decisions. In this paper we present a comparative study where we investigate smart cities in Denmark, Holland, USA, Australia and New Zealand. Our paper focus on how City Managers make decisions surrounding the application of smart city technologies and the data arising. We derive a framework of six barriers to overcome and five leadership roles that needs to be enacted to realize the future sustainable smart city.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Cranefield, Jocelyn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-557091"],"event":{"end":"2018-11-29","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2018-11-28","title":"Transforming for Sustainability","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["New Zealand"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Victoria University of Wellington"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"smart leadership for smart cities a leadership role framework","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/63984360/20181119_Smart_City_paper_for_Transforming_for_Sustainability_conference_Final.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-557091","ids":["ruc-10a151e3-9d48-4fc2-8863-22655d61f690"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AB3776FCFEE052B138BF1F597EDF0BF0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/63984360/20181119_Smart_City_paper_for_Transforming_for_Sustainability_conference_Final.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nz","key":"victoria university of wellington","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Victoria University of Wellington","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jocelyn","key":"cranefieldpau","last":"Cranefield","name":"Cranefield, Jocelyn","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-10a151e3-9d48-4fc2-8863-22655d61f690"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Smart Leadership for Smart Cities : A Leadership Role Framework","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-557091","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Despite significant research into why IT projects fail, the frequency and impact of failure remains high. Attention has shifted to understanding and guiding de-escalation (i.e., reversing failure). This major turnaround process initially benefits from negative feedback on the status quo and requires an organization to break its established frames and re-establish its legitimacy with stakeholders (Pan & Pan, 2011). We consider the role of satire as a lens to challenge dominant frames and better understand stakeholders during the shift towards de-escalation based on analyzing political cartoons about high-profile troubled public sector projects in New Zealand and Denmark. Drawing on the theories of technological frames of reference, legitimacy, and stakeholder salience, we show how cartoonists expose and critique the normative framing of dysfunctionality to act as field-level evaluators of legitimacy. Through counter-framing, exaggeration, and metaphor, they emphasize the urgency of citizen users’ claims while undermining the legitimacy of powerful stakeholders. We extract lessons for stakeholder management and communication during project turnaround and suggest that satire could be a valuable addition to diagnostic and planning tools during de-escalation. We identify that sensitivity to framing of IT projects exists in the public realm, which reinforces calls for organizations to consider institutional framing.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Cranefield, Jocelyn","Oliver, Gillian","Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-560777"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","New Zealand"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Monash University","Victoria University of Wellington"],"keyword":["Cartoons","De escalation","Escalation","Technological frames of reference"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"political satire and the counter framing of public sector it project escalation","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-560777","identifier":[{"id":"85052634673","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-47e47a57-2a75-49dc-a5eb-ae10e34b7466"],"keyword":["Cartoons","De-escalation","Escalation","Political satire","Technological frames of reference"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A5027077DD45B3DE10B824BAB5E8F3D9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nz","key":"victoria university of wellington","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Victoria University of Wellington","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"monash university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Monash University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jocelyn","key":"cranefieldpau","last":"Cranefield","name":"Cranefield, Jocelyn","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Gillian","key":"oliverpau","last":"Oliver","name":"Oliver, Gillian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.17705/1cais.04307","issn":["15293181"],"issue":"1","journal":"Communications of the Association for Information Systems","pages":"133-158","paperid":"7","status":"p","title":"Communications of the Association for Information Systems","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85052634673"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-47e47a57-2a75-49dc-a5eb-ae10e34b7466"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Political Satire and the Counter-framing of Public Sector IT Project Escalation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-560777","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Recognizing that information systems (IS) can have an effect on the envi-ronment, research concerned with the design and development of innovative organizational and technical artifacts has started to focus on the development of ‘sustainable IS’. Much of this work implicitly assumes a focus on the nat-ural environment – our planet. In this paper we propose a broader and more inclusive view of ‘environmental sustainability’ and develop a theory of en-vironmentally sustainable IS development that embodies not only the plane-tary environment but also environments such as that of the organizational setting in which an IS operates. Our design theory offers four new design principles for the development of information systems that support conser-vation, restoration and resilience as sustainability fit functions. We embed these principles into a procedural model of IS development that offers pre-scription in three core stages for design and action","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Baskerville, Richard L.","Recker, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-565017"],"event":{"end":"2018-08-08","place":"Odder, dk","start":"2018-08-05","title":"41st Information Systems Research in Scandinavia Conference","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University","University of Cologne"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing sustainable information systems","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-565017","ids":["ruc-86674c11-aa2c-498e-b7f9-1e6749068213"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7F0F34AB9520F3462DC8A3AD4232D716"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university of cologne","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cologne","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Richard L.","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard L.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jan","key":"reckerpau","last":"Recker","name":"Recker, Jan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-86674c11-aa2c-498e-b7f9-1e6749068213"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Designing Sustainable Information Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-565017","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"I dette kapitel sammenfatter vi kort de trends, vi kan se ud fra undersøgelsen, så de er lettilgængelige for den travle læser.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Bucka-Lassen, Dirk Bredgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-559169"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"trends for projektledelse anno 000000002018","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dra","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.mannaz.com/da/konsulentydelser/program-og-projektledelse/projektlederundersoegelsen-2018/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-559169","ids":["ruc-2fe37f93-eea0-42f5-b974-115ed7ffdc1d"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EC3EB6C13DFED00FBF3ECB60ECAE1F2C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.mannaz.com/da/konsulentydelser/program-og-projektledelse/projektlederundersoegelsen-2018/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Mannaz A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Dirk Bredgaard","key":"buckalassenpau","last":"Bucka-Lassen","name":"Bucka-Lassen, Dirk Bredgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dirk Bredgaard","key":"buckalassenpedh","last":"Bucka-Lassen","name":"Bucka-Lassen, Dirk Bredgaard","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mogens Frank","key":"mikkelsenpedh","last":"Mikkelsen","name":"Mikkelsen, Mogens Frank","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepedh","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Keld","key":"bødkerpedh","last":"Bødker","name":"Bødker, Keld","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"6-7","place":"Hørsholm","publisher":"Mannaz AS","publisher_org":"Mannaz A/S","status":"p","subtitle":"Projektlederundersøgelsen 2018","title":"Hvordan går det ProjektDanmark 2018?"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Roskilde University","Universities","mannaz a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-2fe37f93-eea0-42f5-b974-115ed7ffdc1d"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Trends for projektledelse anno 2018","type":"Report Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-559169","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Denne publikation bygger på en tilbagevendende undersøgelse, som forrige gang blev gennemført i 2014. Undersøgelsen er en af de mest dybdegående undersøgelser, som i år bygger på svar fra 1.740 respondenter – mere end en tredobling af antallet i 2014 – der bredt repræsenterer forskellige brancher. Respondentgruppen er ligeledes repræsenteret bredt i forskellige projekttyper dog med en lille overvægt af it- og udviklingsprojekter. Vi dykker ned i nogle af de mest aktuelle emner inden for projektledelse: kompleksitet, agilitet og projektgevinstrealisering. Resultaterne af undersøgelsen finder du i de efterfølgende kapitler, hvor vi starter med en sammenfatning af de mest centrale observationer i 1. kapitel om trends for projektledelse anno 2018.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Bødker, Keld","Bucka-Lassen, Dirk Bredgaard","Mikkelsen, Mogens Frank"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-561108"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hvordan går det projektdanmark projektlederundersøgelsen 000000002018","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.mannaz.com/da/konsulentydelser/program-og-projektledelse/projektlederundersoegelsen-2018/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-561108","ids":["ruc-4ce46409-5af1-456a-a7be-988c7921e511"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8E03186F6469A2AEB1BCAFCCB3F981F7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.mannaz.com/da/konsulentydelser/program-og-projektledelse/projektlederundersoegelsen-2018/","version":"Published Version"}],"org