h?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-571314","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In the last decades, research in project management (PM) has experienced significant new inputs from a range of new PM methodologies and critical research streams. As a consequence, members of the more critical streams have called for the education of project managers to advance from that of training technicians, to fostering reflective practitioners that are better equipped to handle the increasing complexity of the profession. This paper is based on a recently commenced re-search project titled \"Rethinking Project Management Education – the Role of Universities\" that is aimed at analysing how the development of PM research is reflected in the education of project managers. On the basis of a short overview of the state of the art of PM education research and practices, the possible challenges for the development of PM education are discussed, and, finding that there is a lack of integrated approaches to developing “early reflective practice”, the paper concludes by pointing to possible future research areas to further this development.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Leimbach, Timo","Goodall, Julie Bladt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-182746"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the relation between project management education and newer streams in project management research","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-182746","ids":["au-5d9f389d-2835-4594-8523-e4dd5fb1f63a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3F5D703201CB2B59CAAA6019BF4CCDF7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Centre for Science-Technology-Society Studies","Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Information Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Timo","key":"leimbachpau","last":"Leimbach","locid":"3a2bf281-fff9-4e37-b210-b35b1955e5fc","name":"Leimbach, Timo","orcid":"0000-0001-8483-1634","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Julie Bladt","key":"goodallpau","last":"Goodall","locid":"0cde95ea-1f1c-406f-96f2-8b0ee473d668","name":"Goodall, Julie Bladt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Magnus R. P.","key":"hansenpedh","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Magnus R. P.","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepedh","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788788361094"],"pages":"65-74","publisher":"Roskilde University","status":"p","title":"The future of project management"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5d9f389d-2835-4594-8523-e4dd5fb1f63a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The relation between project management education and newer streams in project management research","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-182746","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Project Portfolio Management (PPM) focus on the integration and alignment of projects with the business operation in order to achieve most value and cost-efficiency for the investment in projects. PPM is often a challenge and especially so for improvement projects where PPM is considerably underdeveloped. In this paper, we present an approach that combines the ImprovAbility model and assessment with a version of a CMMI assessment developed by the Danish company Whitebox. This approach was developed in the world-leading Wind Turbine Company Vestas. The paper presents and discusses this new way of evaluating a portfolio of improvement projects and combine this evaluation with the effect they have on the CMMI maturity level. Further, the paper demonstrates how the combination of a strong senior management requirement for improved maturity and the focus on getting the most value out of PPM made it possible for Vestas to become “better at getting better”.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Jakobsen, Peter M.","Korsaa, Morten","Johansen, Jørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-558008"],"event":{"acronym":"EuroSPI","end":"2017-09-08","place":"Ostrava, cz","start":"2017-09-06","title":"24th European Conference on Software Process Improvement","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CMMI","ImprovAbility","Improvement","Maturity","Process improvement","Success with improvement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH","DI-PR-VES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-PR-VES","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improving project portfolio management ppm for improvement projects","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/64142149/EuroSPI_IA_and_CMMI_v12.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-558008","identifier":[{"id":"85030653597","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-1debc892-b879-4ec8-a1c8-97402548c5c1"],"keyword":["CMMI","ImprovAbility","Improvement","Maturity","Process improvement","Success with improvement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A717FA5DA2D397BAE2AEF3DE1DB4EFD0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/64142149/EuroSPI_IA_and_CMMI_v12.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"vestas","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-VES","l3nl":"Vestas Wind Systems","l3nn":"Vestas","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Vestas","namevar":["Vestas Windsystems, Aarhus, Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-VES","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Whitebox"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejejanpau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter M.","key":"jakobsenpetermpau","last":"Jakobsen","name":"Jakobsen