{"abstract":"Purpose The purpose of this paper is to use translation theory to develop a framework (called FTRA) that explains how companies adopt agile methods in a discourse of fragmentation and articulation. Design/methodology/approach A qualitative multiple case study of six firms using the Scrum agile methodology. Data were collected using mixed methods and analyzed using three progressive coding cycles and analytic induction. Findings In practice, people translate agile methods for local settings by choosing fragments of the method and continuously re-articulating them according to the exact needs of the time and place. The authors coded the fragments as technological rules that share relationships within a framework spanning two dimensions: static-dynamic and actor-artifact. Research limitations/implications For consistency, the six cases intentionally represent one instance of agile methodology (Scrum). This limits the confidence that the framework is suitable for other kinds of methodologies. Practical implications The FTRA framework and the technological rules are promising for use in practice as a prescriptive or even normative frame for governing methodology adaptation. Social implications Framing agile adaption with translation theory surfaces how the discourse between translocal (global) and local practice yields the social construction of agile methods. This result contrasts the more functionalist engineering perspective and privileges changeability over performance. Originality/value The use of translation theory and the FTRA framework to explain how agile adaptation (in particular Scrum) emerges continuously in a process where method fragments are articulated and re-articulated to momentarily suit the local setting. Complete agility that rapidly and elegantly changes its own environment must, as a concomitant, rapidly and elegantly change itself. This understanding also elaborates translation theory by explaining how the articulation and re-articulation of ideas embody the means by which ideas travel in practice.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Baskerville, Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-556684"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University"],"keyword":["Adoption","Agile computing","Case study","Discourse analysis","Information systems development ISD","Organizational change"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the translation and adaptation of agile methods a discourse of fragmentation and articulation","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-556684","identifier":[{"id":"85020220150","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-0a3a0517-1c29-4b88-a067-127495fc9ca5"],"keyword":["Adoption","Agile computing","Case study","Discourse analysis","Information systems development (ISD)","Organizational change"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1855F0D884D24408498C0FABB1348D81"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Richard","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1108/itp-08-2013-0151","issn":["09593845","17585813"],"issn_org":["09593845"],"issue":"2","journal":"Information Technology and People","pages":"396-423","status":"p","title":"Information Technology and People","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020220150"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-0a3a0517-1c29-4b88-a067-127495fc9ca5"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"The Translation and Adaptation of Agile Methods : A Discourse of Fragmentation and Articulation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-556684","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"How do you make the agile organization? Tis paper gives an answer in form of a case story from the financial software company SimCorp. In late 2015SimCorp decided to go agile on a big scale. To do so they applied the scalable agile framework SAFe. In this framework Scrum teams are working within \"Agile Release Trains\" providing value streams that together realize a strategic mission. At SimCorp there were more than 500 employees in 55 teams working in eight agile release trains. SimCorp has a solid track record of releasing a new version of their standard sofware product - SimCorp Dimension - every 6 months. In February 2017 a new version of the product was successfully released according to plan and now with an agile organization behind it. The paper tells the story from beginning to end focusing on the three things that made it possible to become an agile organization within a year. Furthermore the paper discusses what the main challenges were.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Krohn, Malene M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-563635"],"event":{"end":"2017-05-26","place":"Köln, de","start":"2017-05-22","title":"XP2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agile software development","Scaled agile framework"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["SimCorp"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the safe way to the agile organization","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-563635","identifier":[{"id":"85029868402","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-72166462-d30e-49a8-8351-7dcdf52a68a6"],"keyword":["Agile software development","Large-scale software development","Scaled agile framework"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8C4215F1682330D94C58E06AA8F5E45E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["SimCorp"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Malene M.","key":"krohnpau","last":"Krohn","name":"Krohn, Malene M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3120459.3120478","eisbn":["9781450352642"],"place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"XP '17 Workshops Proceedings of the Scientific Workshops of XP2017"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85029868402"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-72166462-d30e-49a8-8351-7dcdf52a68a6"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"The SAFe way to the Agile Organization","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-563635","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Sidste år på Symposiet Projektledelse 2015 afholdt vi for første gang en forskningskonference, som en del af symposiet. Der viste sig at være rigtig stor interesse blandt praktikere i at diskutere de nyeste forskningsresultater med forskerne selv, især med fokus på hvordan resultaterne kan omsættes til praksis. Derfor har vi igen i 2016 planlagt en forskningskonference som en integreret del af Symposiet","author_count":2,"contributors":["Svejvig, Per","Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-194198"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"forskningskonference et unikt forum for vidensdeling mellem teori og praksis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://issuu.com/danskprojektledelse/docs/02-2016_tidsskriftet","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-194198","ids":["au-71943fdb-c9c7-4318-bf98-f0edb5b94218"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C3677928BB580D21AEEC87F02D3621BD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://issuu.com/danskprojektledelse/docs/02-2016_tidsskriftet","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denm