{"abstract":"Professor ved CBIT ved Roskilde Universitet, Jan Pries-Heje, skriver i et debatindlæg, at man burde have forudset en række af de fejlslagne IT-projekter i den offentlige sektor. De fejlslagne projekter har kostet borgerne milliarder, hvor PolSag alene tegnede sig for en regning på 567 millioner kr. Jan Pries-Heje kritiserer politikernes tro på, at man kunne udvikle med udgangspunkt i en række standardsystemer og ud fra Best Practice. Det kan man dog ikke gøre i store og komplekse projekter, fortæller han. I stedet efterlyser Jan Pries-Heje mere fleksibilitet og brugervenlighed","author_count":1,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-559451"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"debat eksperimenter sådan undgår vi nye it skandaler","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-559451","ids":["ruc-33fdcd29-b89f-466c-a0d6-ced768b84a20"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-19CDF48B2BFDCB9FF7E01F03630BDEC0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09071814"],"newspaper":"Politiken","pages":"6","status":"p","title":"Politiken"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-33fdcd29-b89f-466c-a0d6-ced768b84a20"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Debat: Eksperimenter. Sådan undgår vi nye it-skandaler","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-559451","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This paper discusses and defines the achievement of significance in design science research. We review the values and processes of old-science and how this mode of science attacks the complexity of scientific knowledge production through analysis. We then explain how new-science attacks the complexity of scientific knowledge production through synthesis. The work argues that significance of the new-science contribution in design science can be obfuscated when wrapped in old-science. This understanding helps reveal how new-science, such as design science research, constitutes its significance. This discussion translates an old-science framework of theory significance into a new-science framework and uses two published cases to illustrate the framework. The results offer a grounding on which design science research can realize its potential as both new-science and old-science.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Baskerville, Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-567234"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-15","place":"Istanbul, tr","start":"2016-06-12","title":"Twenty-Fourth European Conference on Information Systems (ECIS)","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University"],"keyword":["Paradigm"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discovering the significance of scientific design practice new science wrapped in old science","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-567234","identifier":[{"id":"84995772072","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-a6fb18fd-c423-4c64-9c48-8908abd87b9c"],"keyword":["Design science research method","Paradigm","Pragmatist philosophy","Wrappers"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-72E4B97B83AF3A8C69D9C7FE8F98EB10"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Richard","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00000034"],"journal":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems","status":"p","title":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems","title_org":"Proceedings of the European Conference on Information Systems","volume":"2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-a6fb18fd-c423-4c64-9c48-8908abd87b9c"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Discovering the Significance of Scientific Design Practice : New-Science wrapped in Old Science?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-567234","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Value from ICT Innovation may come from the building of social capital through relational coordination. Hence, for innovation-based companies, combining social capital and economic capital value through the creation and maintenance of business relationships and networking to obtain value plays a central role for their growth and survival. In this paper we design and evaluate a so-called “network nexus” prototype as an ICT value assessment tool for facilitators of innovation-oriented networks. To determine whether a business network is structured for providing value to its members, the facilitator scores the network based on a survey. The scoring of the nexus gives an indication of what to improve to increase value. Evaluation of the nexus resulted in the identification of six types of networks each with their own potential for value. We conclude that design challenges for ICT assessment tools of business network groups can be overcome but needs to be rooted in their context.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-568925"],"event":{"end":"2016-08-10","place":"Ljungskile, se","start":"2016-08-07","title":"Scandinavian Conference on Information Systems","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design science research","Innovation","Network groups","Nexus","Value"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"net up your innovation value","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-568925","identifier":[{"id":"84981320383","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-c0b66b62-2cb3-43ed-a800-3308c397cac2"],"keyword":["Design science research","Innovation","Network groups","Nexus","Value"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AE33BE3F210ED0D5115493EC9A425244"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Magnus Rotvit Perlt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d9c2134a-0799-45eb-8a15-e0523fc96da2","name":"Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ulrika Lundh","key":"snispedh","last":"Snis","name":"Snis, Ulrika Lundh","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-43597-8_6","isbn":["9783319435961"],"issn":["18651348"],"pages":"70-85","place":"Schweiz","publisher":"Springer VS","series":"Lecture Notes in Business Information Processing","status":"p","subtitle":"7th Scandinavian Conference on Information Systems, SCIS 2016 and IFIP8.6 2016, Ljungskile, Sweden, August 7-10, 2016, Proceedings","title":"Nordic Contributions in IS Research"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84981320383"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-c0b66b62-2cb3-43ed-a800-3308c397cac2"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Net up your innovation value","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-568925","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Project Half Double is an industry-driven initiative with the purpose to develop a new and radical project paradigm to increase the competitiveness of the Danish industry. The research part of Project Half Double will assess the degree to which the new project paradigm is more successful than traditional approaches, which calls for an evaluation and comparison framework. This paper describes the design of such a comparison framework consisting of the five elements context, project, mechanism/practices, output and impact based on the open systems view. We illustrate the use of the comparison framework for front-loading projects in Grundfos and the specific evaluation criteria used here. The design and use of comparison frameworks have some implications such as it being challenging to define relevant and meaningful evaluation criteria, it is difficult to collect complex evaluation data, and some organizations lack the project maturity to take advantage of the frameworks.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Svejvig, Per","Hedegaard, Flemming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-227689"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-09","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2016-06-08","title":"Second Danish Project Management Research Conference","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-GFS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-GFS","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the challenges of evaluating and comparing projects an empirical study of designing a comparison framework","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-227689","ids":["au-ac7b4258-78ca-4b1a-9517-595eaaca465f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-473E1F83C07E83C76B995B5E6B11382C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"grundfos","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-GFS","l3nl":"Grundfos","l3nn":"Grundfos","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Grundfos","namevar":["Grundfos A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-GFS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"svejvigpau","last":"Svejvig","locid":"40558617-c35b-464e-a0f6-7a2940494271","name":"Svejvig, Per","orcid":"0000-0002-8758-4031","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming","key":"hedegaardpau","last":"Hedegaard","name":"Hedegaard, Flemming","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepedh","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Per","key":"svejvigpedh","last":"Svejvig","name":"Svejvig, Per","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788778674944"],"isbn":["9788778674845"],"pages":"107-129","publisher":"Roskilde Universitetsforlag","status":"p","title":"Project Management for Achieving Change"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Grundfos","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ac7b4258-78ca-4b1a-9517-595eaaca465f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The challenges of evaluating and comparing projects : An empirical study of designing a comparison framework","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-227689","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Although the importance of creativity in design science research projects has been widely acknowledged, efforts to facilitate this creativity while ensuring rigor, have been largely overlooked. This paper presents a more thorough understanding of creativity in design science research, balancing it with scientific rigor and addressing practical problems. With this objective, we analyze creativity within design science research and find that, although creativity is generally associated with \"outside the box\" thinking, creativity can also be effectively applied within the constraints of problem-solving. We develop a framework explicating how bounded creativity supports both, the design process, as well as the development of innovative artifacts. The framework is evaluated using a design science research project that develops a method for designing creative pervasive games. This research makes a novel contribution by demonstrating how creativity can be induced within the structure of the design science research methodology.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Baskerville, Richard","Storey, Veda","Kaul, Mala","Kristiansen, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-558682"],"event":{"end":"2016-12-14","place":"Dublin, ie","start":"2016-12-11","title":"Thirty Seventh International Conference on Information Systems","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University","University of Nevada, Reno"],"keyword":["Bounded creativity","Creativity","Design science research","Designing","Rigor","Site storming","Theorizing"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-KUM"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-KUM","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bounded creativity in design science research","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-558682","identifier":[{"id":"85019443546","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-28c5dab6-f694-48b1-b31a-a8f85b8bd3f4"],"keyword":["Bounded creativity","Creativity","Design science research","Designing","Rigor","Site-storming","Theorizing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8E876A5CDF6C7C387DECEFB6D224FED7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of nevada reno","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Nevada, Reno","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"kum ministry of culture archives museums and royal library denmark","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-KUM","l3nn":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","namevar":["Museum Lolland-Falster"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-KUM","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Richard","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Veda","key":"storeypau","last":"Storey","name":"Storey, Veda","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Mala","key":"kaulpau","last":"Kaul","name":"Kaul, Mala","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Erik","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00000033"],"journal":"Proceedings of the International Conference on Information Systems","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the International Conference on Information Systems","volume":"December 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-28c5dab6-f694-48b1-b31a-a8f85b8bd3f4"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Bounded Creativity in Design Science Research","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-558682","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This paper addresses the design problem of designing IS tools for supporting inter-organizational innovation network groups. Inter-organizational networks are groups of people with diverse backgrounds and interests. Innovation networks consist of rationalized structures and socially constructed processes that are ongoing over long periods of time and is thus a highly complex problem. We argue that in order to design such IS artifacts well, we need design principles for constructing future IS artifacts. From the experiences of designing and evaluating a Group-focused Engagement & Network Innovation Environment (GENIE) nexus tool based on design science research, we propose five general design principles that aid how to design and utilize such IS tools when one plays a role in a innovation network group either as a member, facilitator or network sponsor. Our contribution is a proposal of a GENIE design theory as the foundation for future development of IS artifacts.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt","Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-569521"],"event":{"acronym":"DESRIST","end":"2016-05-25","place":"St. John’s, ca","start":"2016-05-24","title":"Design Science research in Information Systems and Technology (DESRIST)","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"out of the bottle design principles for genie tools","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-569521","identifier":[{"id":"85007154202","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-c98f4657-ce32-42fc-80ed-e6c9255616c1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F5C4904888F4E03F1827EFFC48C6116B"],"org"