{"abstract":"More and more software firms adopt agile methods into their practice to become more flexible and increase their speed to market. To get the best from both worlds, they often choses to balance agility with traditional approaches. This complicates the job for especially the project managers. This paper investigates the new project manager role of balanced systems development by building a theoretically based framework and render it probable through two case studies. The paper describes the complexity of the new role and how it may lead to overload of the project manager. Solutions inspired by agility and ambidexterity are sketched.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Tjørnehøj, Gitte","Jespersen, Andreas Saxkjær","von Moos, Theis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-051250"],"event":{"end":"2016-05-21","place":"København, dk","start":"2016-05-20","title":"1st Danish Project Management Research Conference","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Bankdata"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"are all we need heroes the new role of the it project manager the new role of the it project manager","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-051250","ids":["aau-0433a612-68ac-4653-b4f2-f90c71b6a966"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E23ACEE180215BBF86A8B6F7AFD09602"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, Centre for Information Systems Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Bankdata"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gitte","key":"tjørnehøjpau","last":"Tjørnehøj","locid":"0c313b43-1daa-4d6a-8b70-463c557e4b82","name":"Tjørnehøj, Gitte","orcid":"0000-0002-3630-5688","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Saxkjær","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","name":"Jespersen, Andreas Saxkjær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Theis","key":"vonmoospau","last":"von Moos","name":"von Moos, Theis","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepedh","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Per","key":"svejvigpedh","last":"Svejvig","name":"Svejvig, Per","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788778674661"],"place":"Samfundslitteratur","status":"p","title":"Project Management Theory Meets Practice"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0433a612-68ac-4653-b4f2-f90c71b6a966"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Are All We Need Heroes? -The New Role of the IT-Project Manager : -The New Role of the IT-Project Manager","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-051250","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Design science research should be relevant, valuable, purposeful and prescriptive. Its value as a relevant source of prescriptions implies the practical usefulness of its results beyond a single expository instantiation. But propagation of such design science products as design principles and theories appears to be a key challenge. In this paper we commence with a DESRIST paper from 2012 that instantiated design principles in an artifact for a bank. That paper included plans and techniques for future use of its principles (propagation), including prescriptions for a five-phase adoption process. In this paper we discuss the propagation issues around generalizing design science research across multiple contexts and propose alternative propagation concepts of projectability and entrenchment. The existing concepts around generalizability have issues that make them less suitable for design science research: context (local/possible worlds) and theoretical statements based on functional explanations. A projection is any relevant instance that supports a theory. Projectability involves defining the relationship between a base case or evidence and a projection. Entrenchment occurs when design principles or theories have stimulated many actual projections. We demonstrate these concepts in a case study of propagation: a chemical manufacturer and service provider that adopted the design principles arising from that 2012 DESRIST banking-based design science research. We conclude that generalizability is too well-oriented to descriptive research and argue that a more appropriate framing for design science research is projectability and entrenchment. The paper includes recommendations to increase the projectability of design science research.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Baskerville, Richard","Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383379"],"event":{"acronym":"DESRIST","title":"Design Science Research in Information Systems and Technology"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design science research","Entrenchment","Generalizability","Projectability","Propagation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"projecting the future for design science research an action case based analysis","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84937468962","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383379","identifier":[{"id":"84937468962","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8f605610-22cb-4d96-b270-686e43b45099"],"keyword":["Design Science Research","Entrenchment","Generalizability","Projectability","Propagation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-2532310EFEF891A2F7DC6DA44871D589"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-18714-3_18","eisbn":["9783319187136"],"isbn":["9783319187143"],"issn":["03029743"],"publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"10th International Conference, DESRIST 2015, Dublin, Ireland, May 20-22, 2015, Proceedings","title":"New Horizons in Design Science: Broadening the Research Agenda"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84937468962"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8f605610-22cb-4d96-b270-686e43b45099"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Projecting the Future for Design Science Research: An Action‐Case Based Analysis","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383379","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The workplace is changing rapidly and knowledge work is conducted increasingly in settings that are global, digital, flat and networked. The epicenter of value-creation are the individuals and their interactions. Unified Communication and Collaboration Technology (UC&C) supports individual interactions, collaboration and knowledge creation. The use of this technology is growing globally. In a previous study, we found that UC&C in collocated and distributed settings, produced misfits and fits between situated enacted practice-use of UC&C and the experienced productivity. We respond to the KITA 2015 call with this work-in-progress paper. We apply the IT Knowledge Artefact (ITKA)-interpretive lens from Cabitza and Locoro (2014) to a case of knowledge workers struggling with appropriation of UC&C for creating and sharing practice knowledge. We evaluate the framework - and discuss the usefulness of the lens in this specific setting. To further improve and enrich, we pose questions, aiming at contributing to the communication of valuable insights informing the design and use of future ITKAs in knowledge work.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Fischer, Louise Harder","Pries-Heje, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383681"],"event":{"end":"2015-11-14","place":"Lissabon, pt","start":"2015-11-12","title":"7th International Joint Conference on Knowledge Discovery, Knowledge Engineering and Knowledge Management","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["IT knowledge Artefacts","Individual Practices","Knowledge creation","Situativity","Socio Technical Fit","UC C"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the misfits in knowledge work grasping the essence with the lens of the it knowledge artefact","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84960954273","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383681","identifier":[{"id":"84960954273","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a58dd1be-c2bb-4533-b9c2-18c894ffc8e5"],"keyword":["IT-knowledge Artefacts","Individual Practices","Knowledge Creation","Situativity","Socio-Technical Fit","UC&C"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F617D4FD38E2FD43E6B3D54189E6E3B5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Information Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Harder","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a22e85da-82e3-410d-8ef1-31407362ba19","name":"Fischer, Louise Harder","orcid":"0000-0001-7193-3797","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Lene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ana","key":"fredpedh","last":"Fred","name":"Fred, Ana","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"dietzpedh","last":"Dietz","name":"Dietz, Jan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"aveiropedh","last":"Aveiro","name":"Aveiro, David","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kecheng","key":"liupedh","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Kecheng","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Joaquim","key":"felipepedh","last":"Felipe","name":"Felipe, Joaquim","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5220/0005662204360443","isbn":["9789897581588"],"pages":"436-443","place":"Lisbon - Portugal","publisher":"SCITEPRESS Digital Library","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 7th International Joint Conference on Knowledge Discovery, Knowledge Engineering and Knowledge Management","title":"IC3K 2015","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960954273"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a58dd1be-c2bb-4533-b9c2-18c894ffc8e5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Misfits in Knowledge Work : Grasping the Essence with the Lens of the IT Knowledge Artefact","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383681","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Resultaterne i denne rapport er to værktøjer til at hjælpe facilitatorer med deres virksomhedsnetværksgrupper organiseret af Thy Erhvervsforum (ThyEF). Til designet af værktøjerne har vi anvendt designvidenskabelig metode. Det har været nødvendigt at indsnævre begrebet ”netværk”. Således fokuserer rapporten på hvordan netværk forstået som ”netværksgrupper” bliver organiseret af ”netværksorganisationer” med tilhørende tre interessenter der skal integreres i opstarten af netværksgrupper. Rapporten behandler også kendetegn ved en netværksgruppe og udarbejder en visualisering af seks typer af netværksgrupper baseret på to fokusgruppeinterview med netværksdeltagere og fem individuelle interview med netværksfacilitatorer. De to designede værktøjer er: a) et ”Netværkscharter”; et generisk kommissoriums-dokument til at starte, overdrage og evaluere netværksgruppers formål og succeskriterier, og b) en ”Netværksnexus”; et generisk rammeværk til at skabe overblik og dialog mellem facilitatorer, netværksejere og netværksdeltagere for at kunne bestemme hvilke virkemidler netværksfacilitatoren kan anvende for at udvikle netværket i en ønsket retning. Begge værktøjer bliver evalueret formativt og rapporten diskuterer til sidst potentialet for videreudvikling.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-570069"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"netværks nexus afsluttende rapportering juni 000000002015 thy erhvervsforum","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-570069","ids":["ruc-d1fed8a5-1274-4570-94ee-9460479e231f"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-699A4B1DC7E7A0861A8E67064716745E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation","Roskilde University, The Department of Communication, Business and Information Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Magnus Rotvit Perlt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d9c2134a-0799-45eb-8a15-e0523fc96da2","name":"Hansen, Magnus Rotvit Perlt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"31","place":"Thy","publisher":"Thy Erhvervsforum","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-d1fed8a5-1274-4570-94ee-9460479e231f"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Netværks Nexus : Afsluttende rapportering, juni 2015. Thy Erhvervsforum","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-570069","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Purpose – The purpose of this paper is to suggest that translating a design theory (DT) into practice (e.g. creating an instance design artifact (IDA)) is hardly straight-forward and requires substantial creativity. Specifically the authors suggest that adopting a DT embodies a creativity passdown effect in which the creative thinking of a team of design theorist(s) inherent in DT invokes a creative mind of a team of artifact instance designer(s) in creating an IDA. In this study, the authors empirically investigate the creativity passdown effect through an action case in which a DT (DT nexus) was applied in creating an IDA (multi-outsourcing decision-making tool). Design/methodology/approach – The case methodology applied here is described as an action case. An action case is a hybrid research approach that combines action research and interpretive case approaches. It combines intervention and interpretation in order to achieve both change and understanding. It is a form of soft field experiment with less emphasis on iteration and learning and more on trial and making. The approach is holistic in philosophy, and prediction is not emphasized. The intervention in the case was that of an instance designer team introducing a previously published DT as a basis for creating an IDA. Findings – The experience in the action case suggests that using a DT in creating an IDA may encourage design thinking, and in certain way increase its power and practical relevance by fostering the creative mind of instance designers. Indeed, DTs provide a scientific basis for dealing with an instance problem, and this evokes the creativity mind of instance designers. Without such a scientific basis, it is a lot more challenging for instance artifact designers to deal with instance problems. Research limitations/implications – This study contributes to the literature concerning design science research, as it challenges the notion that adopting scientific design knowledge limits creativity inherent in creating IDA by illustrating creative elements involved in adopting DT as a basis for creating IDAs. Practical implications – This study offers implications to practice, as it provides new insights regarding how DT can be used in instance design activities. Originality/value – A report of this research previously appeared as a conference paper. However, the attached journal version has been completely rewritten to additionally contribute to the literature concerning design science research beyond the conference version. More specifically, in this version, the authors conceptualize adopting a DT to build an IDA as a theoretical basis, and the authors challenge the notion that adopting scientific design knowledge limits creativity inherent in creating IDA by illustrating creative elements involved in executing DT as a basis for creating IDAs.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Lee, Jong Seok","Baskerville, Richard"],"cuid":["S02-094.34-038348"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University"],"keyword":["Action research","Design research","Design science","IT artifact"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the creativity passdown effect applying design theory in creating instance design","src":["itu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84938694466","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-094.34-038348","identifier":[{"id":"84938694466","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-912a3b81-9662-4955-bc30-0effad83669d","ruc-807a0f89-3e6e-45b3-976f-5917ccca35b5"],"keyword":["Action research","Design research","Design science","IT artifact"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-963D8B2C778086A84E42645F2A28FBD6"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jong Seok","key":"leepau","last":"Lee","name":"Lee, Jong Seok","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Richard","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1108/itp-04-2013-0080","issn":["09593845","17585813"],"issn_org":["09593845"],"issue":"3","journal":"Information Technology and People","pages":"529-543","publisher":"Emerald Group Publishing","status":"p","title":"Information Technology and People","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84938694466"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-912a3b81-9662-4955-bc30-0effad83669d","ruc-807a0f89-3e6e-45b3-976f-5917ccca35b5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"The Creativity Passdown Effect : Applying Design Theory in Creating Instance Design","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.34-038348","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Lever forskere i et Elfenbenstårn? Det tror du måske, men nu får du mulighed for ved selvsyn at afgøre at det ikke er tilfældet. Som en del af symposiet 2015 organiserer vi et spor om forskning i projektledelse, hvor du får mulighed for både at møde projektledelses-forskere, og deres resultater.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Svejvig, Per","Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-165663"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"forskerkonference en nyskabelse på symposiet projektledelse 000000002015","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://issuu.com/danskprojektledelse/docs/2015-02_helt_blad","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-165663","ids":["au-3fc83070-e9f6-4eb7-a082-3c699c04c7d4"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C5F6F54CFFC91F0B362D0C5832B45587"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"svejvigpau","last":"Svejvig","locid":"40558617-c35b-464e-a0f6-7a2940494271","name":"Svejvig, Per","orcid":"0000-0002-8758-4031","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19035403"],"issue":"2","journal":"Projektledelse","pages":"10-11","publisher":"Foreningen Dansk Projektledelse","status":"p","title":"Projektledelse","volume":"19"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3fc83070-e9f6-4eb7-a082-3c699c04c7d4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Forskerkonference - en nyskabelse på Symposiet Projektledelse 2015","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-165663","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The ISO/IEC 33014.2013 [1] standard on process improvement includes a core activity called ‘identify the overall change strategy’, which includes selecting a change strategy among the many available. This selection can be carried out using the ImprovAbility model [2] in which there is a framework of how to select change strategy. The framework contains 10 different change strategies to choose from. But which ones are chosen in practice? To answer that, we have analyzed data from 134 assessments in 129 organizations that have used the framework. We give a ranking of strategies chosen, and we analyze how they adapt the change strategy to their specific conditions. We conclude that the most often recommended organizational change strategy is optionality followed by three other strategies: specialist-driven, production-organized, and learning-driven.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Johansen, Jørn"],"cuid":["S02-086.54-672184"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Change strategy","ISO IEC 33014","Organisational change","Process improvement"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"choosing change strategy for iso iec 000000033014","src":["itu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84939555731","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-086.54-672184","identifier":[{"id":"84939555731","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4111f85e-de32-4a94-b011-4a62e0f10e95","ruc-c6efc596-1fd3-49b6-95f1-846bd0c22a13"],"keyword":["ISO/IEC 33014","Organisational change","change strategy","process improvement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-53E81C75FF7FD4EAF7E22E5260B63183"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Whitebox"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørn","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Jørn","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/smr.1724","issn":["20477473","20477481"],"issn_org":["20477473"],"issue":"8","journal":"Journal of Software: Evolution and Process","pages":"573-583","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Journal of Software: Evolution and Process","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84939555731"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Other Companies","Private Research","Roskilde University","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","whitebox"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4111f85e-de32-4a94-b011-4a62e0f10e95","ruc-c6efc596-1fd3-49b6-95f1-846bd0c22a13"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Choosing change strategy for ISO/IEC 33014","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.54-672184","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Process thinking and process-based theory are receiving increased attention in the field of organization studies and organization theory development (Tsoukas & Chia, 2002; Langley & Tsoukas, 2010; Hernes, 2014). The aim has been to study processes rather than structures, in organizations. This has recently inspired research on the organizing of projects and the development of a (new) theory of temporary organizations (Bakker, 2010; Blomquist et al. 2010; Söderlund, 2013). These theories are still under development and need empirical studies that can show their relevance for practice. This paper will give an overview of this theoretical development and discuss the consequences for the practice of project management. The paper finds that the focus on processes such as time and temporality, meaning structures, and articulation are covered in project management research, but sparsely documented outside specific industries. The practical implications and applications have to do with enhancing the role of project manager (PM) from controlling to facilitating, directing, and authoring.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Schlamovitz, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-558165"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Projektledelse"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"theory meets practice practical implications of process theory in project management","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-558165","ids":["ruc-20301ab3-43e9-4cf1-8725-d6e736a49c62"],"keyword":["Projektledelse"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-85ACE88E6F1C1958DC15610006CE760F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Social Sciences and Business, Management and organization","Roskilde University, The Department of Communication, Business and Information Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"schlamovitzpau","last":"Schlamovitz","locid":"9f6bd11c-14a4-4909-8bb9-902e1472a2b3","name":"Schlamovitz, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-1408-9021","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepedh","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Per","key":"svejvigpedh","last":"Svejvig","name":"Svejvig, Per","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788778674616"],"place":"Roskilde","publisher":"Samfundslitteratur","status":"p","title":"Project Management Theory Meets Practice"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-20301ab3-43e9-4cf1-8725-d6e736a49c62"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Theory Meets Practice : Practical Implications of Process Theory in Project Management","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-558165","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Crowston, Kevin","Devos, Jan","Ramos, Isabel","Kasper, George M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-571121"],"event":{"end":"2015-10-07","place":"Daejeon, kr","start":"2015-10-04","title":"23rd IFIP World Computer Congress","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"big data information systems tc 000000000008 track ifip world computer conference daejeon korea 000000000004 000000000007 october 000000002015","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-571121","identifier":[{"id":"84930860907","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-e10ec8ef-69e3-4a9c-a2e7-b873a3a2fdff"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-69A51AAD30F520CA638540B435ADA25A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation","Roskilde University, The Department of Communication, Business and Information Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejeped","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","first":"Kevin","key":"crowstonped","last":"Crowston","name":"Crowston, Kevin","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"devosped","last":"Devos","name":"Devos, Jan","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","first":"Isabel","key":"ramosped","last":"Ramos","name":"Ramos, Isabel","rank":4,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","first":"George M.","key":"kasperped","last":"Kasper","name":"Kasper, George M.","rank":5,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"pages":"45","place":"Daejeon, Korea","publisher":"IFIP Int. Federation for Information Processing","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-e10ec8ef-69e3-4a9c-a2e7-b873a3a2fdff"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Big Data Information Systems : TC 8 track. IFIP World Computer Conference. Daejeon. Korea. 4 - 7 October 2015","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-571121","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Design science research should be relevant, valuable, purposeful and prescriptive. Its value as a relevant source of prescriptions implies the practical usefulness of its results beyond a single expository instantiation. But propagation of such design science products as design principles and theories appears to be a key challenge. In this paper we commence with a DESRIST paper from 2012 that instantiated design principles in an artifact for a bank. That paper included plans and techniques for future use of its principles (propagation), including prescriptions for a five-phase adoption process. In this paper we discuss the propagation issues around generalizing design science research across multiple contexts and propose alternative propagation concepts of projectability and entrenchment. The existing concepts around generalizability have issues that make them less suitable for design science research: context (local/possible worlds) and theoretical statements based on functional explanations. A projection is any relevant instance that supports a theory. Projectability involves defining the relationship between a base case or evidence and a projection. Entrenchment occurs when design principles or theories have stimulated many actual projections. We demonstrate these concepts in a case study of propagation: a chemical manufacturer and service provider that adopted the design principles arising from that 2012 DESRIST banking-based design science research. We conclude that generalizability is too well-oriented to descriptive research and argue that a more appropriate framing for design science research is projectability and entrenchment. The paper includes recommendations to increase the projectability of design science research.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Baskerville, Richard","Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-571358"],"event":{"end":"2015-05-22","place":"Dublin, ie","start":"2015-05-20","title":"10th International Conference","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"projecting the future for design science research an action case based analysis","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-571358","identifier":[{"id":"84937468962","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-e4b6b44e-5eaa-4fda-b198-0addd479647a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-2532310EFEF891A2F7DC6DA44871D589"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation","Roskilde University, The Department of Communication, Business and Information Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Richard","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Brian","key":"donnellanpedh","last":"Donnellan","name":"Donnellan, Brian","rank":3,"rol