{"abstract":"This paper reveals how project program management can aim for lifetime sustainability of offshore windmill parks through innovation. The research is based on a qualitative focus group interview with 11 enterprises and 6 individual semi-constructed interviews with 6 enterprises. Offshore windmill parks are revealed to be complex product systems (CoPS), and this context has an important impact on the structuring of project program management. The findings show a need for the “frontload” of resources in the early stage of project program management. This structure is different from the widely used Stage Gate sequential structuring with typical load of resources in the final stages. A model is developed for structuring programs of windmill parks emphasizing “frontload” on coordination of uncertainty and complexness, creativity and control and integration of relationships. This paper contributes to existing project management literature on CoPS.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Brink, Tove"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-592438"],"event":{"end":"2015-05-21","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2015-05-20","title":"1st Danish Project Management Research Conference","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Complex Product Systems CoPS","Innovation","Levelised cost of energy LCOE","Project management","Sustainability"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"frontload in complex project program management to aim for lifetime sustainability of offshore windmill parks","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://samfundslitteratur.dk/bog/project-management-theory-meets-practice","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-592438","ids":["sdu-4304b075-22be-478f-ba9b-df2329063493"],"keyword":["Complex Product Systems (CoPS)","Levelised cost of energy (LCOE)","Project Management","innovation","sustainability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-242AAB827712BBF36C8759A94F1D72C1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Sociology, Environmental and Business Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tove","key":"brinkpau","last":"Brink","locid":"4767043a-dec0-4b2b-ae68-4757cbb3b493","name":"Brink, Tove","orcid":"0000-0003-0524-9211","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepedh","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Per","key":"svejvigpedh","last":"Svejvig","name":"Svejvig, Per","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1.","eisbn":["9788778674661"],"isbn":["9788778674616"],"pages":"73-85","publisher":"Roskilde Universitetsforlag","status":"p","title":"Project Management Theory Meets Practice"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-4304b075-22be-478f-ba9b-df2329063493"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"“Frontload” in complex project program management to aim for lifetime sustainability of offshore windmill parks","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-592438","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"A recent survey shows that 40% of all projects use, or have used, agile methods. The most commonly used agile method is Scrum, one reason being that Scrum provides mechanisms for building a healthy temporal environment for the project participants. Through a case study carried out in a Danish municipality we demkonstrate how the tgemporal environment in a project is influenced - enhanced as well as challenged - by the use of Scrum.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Scheller, Vibeke Kristine","Hvid, Helge Søndergaard","Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S02-084.21-038260"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Agile methods","Case study","Project management","Scrum","Temporal environment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fast or smart how the use of scrum can influence the temporal environment in a project","src":["itu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-084.21-038260","ids":["itu-18211119-4f9e-49b0-a42a-90d3c725776c","ruc-c35705e8-fd2c-4ee0-ac4f-f96c48f9a396"],"keyword":["Agile methods","Case study","Project management","Scrum","Temporal environment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-5E954D996A58ED0EF31AF6AAE80C361B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Sustainable Working Life","Roskilde University, The Department of Environmental, Social and Spatial Chang