{"abstract":"When you have stable and non-ambiguous requirements then a classic contract for IS between a supplier and a public sector institution based on a requirements specification may be well suited. However, if you have to accept many changes or have ambiguous requirements then you may end up with “endless” re-negotiation of the requirements; you need a more flexible way to develop IS. A new way of coping with many changes is to use an agile development approach and a fixed budget and resources contract. This paper presents an example case. We analyse the case and design a guideline for how to implement a fixed budget and resources contract in the public sector. The guideline includes elements to cope with challenges in a tender process such as transparency, criteria for supplier selection, and live assessment of resource skills and capabilities, as well as achieving the flexibility for change needed.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Lene","Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381501"],"event":{"acronym":"IRIS","title":"Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design science research","Public sector","agile resource contract","tender process"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"agile contracts designing an agile team selection guideline","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://aisel.aisnet.org/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1011&context=iris2014","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381501","ids":["itu-0fe81fd7-6de9-435a-bac0-ac58d4937d66"],"keyword":["Design science research","agile resource contract","public sector","tender process"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-71E7AF26E40EB384E87E019DDA2689E6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://aisel.aisnet.org/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1011&context=iris2014","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://aisel.aisnet.org/iris2014/%20","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Interdisciplinary Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"prieshejelenepau","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Lene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"prieshejejanpau","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18919863","23873353"],"issn_org":["18919863"],"journal":"IRIS: Selected Papers of the Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia","pages":"34-49","paperid":"4","publisher":"Scandinavian Chapter of the Association for Information Systems (AIS) - Scandinavian IRIS","status":"p","title":"IRIS: Selected Papers of the Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0fe81fd7-6de9-435a-bac0-ac58d4937d66"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Agile Contracts: Designing an Agile Team Selection Guideline","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381501","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Technological knowledge has been characterized as having a scope that is specific to a particular problem. However, the information systems community is exploring forms of design science research that provide a promising avenue to technological knowledge with broader scope: design theories. Because design science research is materially prescriptive, it requires a different perspective in developing the breadth of applications of design theories. In this paper we propose different concepts that embody forms of general technological knowledge The concept of projectability, developed originally as a means of distinguishing realized generalizations from unrealized generalizations, helps explain how design theories, being prescriptive, possess a different form of applicability. The concept of entrenchment describes the use of a theory in many projections. Together these concepts provide a means for comparative discussions of the importance of design theories. Projectable design theories guide designers in the design of artifacts similar in principle, but different in context. These can also help design researchers understand interrelationships between design theories.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Baskerville, Richard","Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384794"],"event":{"acronym":"IFIP WG82","title":"IFIP WG 8.2 Working Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design Theories","Design science research","Entrenchment","Projectability","Technological Knowledge"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design theory projectability","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84915771184","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384794","identifier":[{"id":"84915771184","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ef840593-771e-41cb-a948-8d32e397e08e"],"keyword":["Design Science Research","Design Theories","Entrenchment","Projectability","Technological Knowledge"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-B47354A924D1645194BF73947881DFC2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-45708-5_14","eisbn":["9783662457085"],"isbn":["9783662457078"],"pages":"219-232","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"IFIP WG 8.2 Working Conference on Information Systems and Organizations, IS&amp;O 2014, Auckland, New Zealand, December 11-12, 2014. Proceedings","title":"Information Systems and Global Assemblages. (Re)Configuring Actors, Artefacts, Organizations"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84915771184"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ef840593-771e-41cb-a948-8d32e397e08e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Design Theory Projectability","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384794","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
