{"abstract":"When you have stable and non-ambiguous requirements then a classic contract for IS between a supplier and a public sector institution based on a requirements specification may be well suited. However, if you have to accept many changes or have ambiguous requirements then you may end up with “endless” re-negotiation of the requirements; you need a more flexible way to develop IS. A new way of coping with many changes is to use an agile development approach and a fixed budget and resources contract. This paper presents an example case. We analyse the case and design a guideline for how to implement a fixed budget and resources contract in the public sector. The guideline includes elements to cope with challenges in a tender process such as transparency, criteria for supplier selection, and live assessment of resource skills and capabilities, as well as achieving the flexibility for change needed.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Pries-Heje, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-569501"],"event":{"end":"2014-08-13","place":"Ringsted, dk","start":"2014-08-10","title":"IRIS 37/SCIS 5","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"agile contracts designing an agile team selection guideline","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://aisel.aisnet.org/iris2014/4/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-569501","ids":["ruc-c948ef8f-c189-496b-9450-9918e7aec59e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1D75F1E1DE612776C448EFF0C60697CC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","