=LOI:S01-000.00-571667","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Outsourcing is now a feasible means for enterprise systems (ES) cost savings, but does however increase the complexity of coordination substantially when many organizations are involved. We set out to study ES outsourcing in a large Scandinavian high-tech organization, SCANDI, a case setting with many inter-organizational partners, trying to answer the question: Why does SCANDI engage in these very complex outsourcing arrangements? To answer this question we have analyzed documents, observed meetings and gathered data from interviews in four parts of SCANDI. The first data analysis found just the rational front stage cost-saving explanation; but then, with a more careful analysis focusing on institutional factors, other backstage explanations “behind the curtain” were uncovered, such as management consultants with a “best practice” agenda, people promoting outsourcing, thereby being promoted themselves, and a belief in outsourcing as a “silver bullet”: a recipe to success, solving everything.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Svejvig, Per","Pries-Heje, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-771648"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enterprise systems outsourcing behind the curtain a case study showing how rational and institutional explanations coexist and complement each other","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105011412328","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-771648","identifier":[{"id":"105011412328","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0a17ac0c-5a07-4fff-b735-09c4f24d63d3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-2CA3A3C936B1308D39181D9626396007"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"svejvigpau","last":"Svejvig","locid":"40558617-c35b-464e-a0f6-7a2940494271","name":"Svejvig, Per","orcid":"0000-0002-8758-4031","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Madjid","key":"tavanapedh","last":"Tavana","name":"Tavana, Madjid","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4018/978-1-4666-2464-1.ch001","isbn":["9781466624641"],"pages":"1-18","publisher":"IGI global","status":"p","title":"Competition, Strategy, and Modern Enterprise Information Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105011412328"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0a17ac0c-5a07-4fff-b735-09c4f24d63d3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Enterprise Systems Outsourcing “Behind the Curtain”: A Case Study Showing How Rational and Institutional Explanations Coexist and Complement Each Other","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-771648","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Payment transactions through the use of physical coins, bank notes or credit cards have for centuries been the standard formats of exchanging money. Recently online and mobile digital payment platforms has entered the stage as contenders to this position and possibly could penetrate societies thoroughly and substitute current payment standards in the decades to come. This paper portrays how digital payment paltforms evolve in socio-technical niches and how various technological platforms aim for institutional attention in their attempt to challenge earlier platforms and standards. The paper applies a co-evolutionary multilevel perspective to model the interplay and processes between technology and society wherein digital payment platforms potentially will substitute other payment platforms just like the credit card negated the check. On this basis this paper formulate a multilevel conceptual framework and shows, through examples of new digital payment platforms, how transitions and substitutions might occur. Finally we discuss how possible venues and routes of transitions appear in the genesis and evolution of digital payment platforms.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten","Damsgaard, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-292855"],"event":{"end":"2012-06-13","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2012-06-10","title":"20th European Conference on Information Systems, ECIS 2012","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital payment platforms","Evolution","Transitions"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genesis and evolution of digital payment platforms","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://aisel.aisnet.org/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1059&context=ecis2012","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-292855","identifier":[{"id":"84905748788","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-b7dcdef6-126c-4cf7-b8e2-ff0a5041f3aa"],"keyword":["Digital payment platforms","Evolution","Technology substitution","Transitions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CFFC82190AB95D81577373F7673C87B7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Intercultural Communication and Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"fdaf290a-0e56-48a5-8afc-dc8d44fdbf3e","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"damsgaardpau","last":"Damsgaard","locid":"97c6e5ec-b082-4a41-a238-69fe8cdf2a1d","name":"Damsgaard, Jan","orcid":"0000-0002-7504-1937","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepedh","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mike","key":"chiassonpedh","last":"Chiasson","name":"Chiasson, Mike","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonathan","key":"warehampedh","last":"Wareham","name":"Wareham, Jonathan","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Xavier","key":"busquetspedh","last":"Busquets","name":"Busquets, Xavier","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Josep","key":"valorpedh","last":"Valor","name":"Valor, Josep","rank":7,"role":"Editor of H