nformation Systems Research In Scandinavia","title_org":"Proceedings / Information Systems Research In Scandinavia (IRIS)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Roskilde University","Universities","danske bank"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-2cdebd54-6c6c-4528-86e9-37754cd8c8d7"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Designing a framework for multi-sourcing decisions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-558969","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Evaluation is a central and essential activity in conducting rigorous Design Science Research (DSR), yet there is surprisingly little guidance about designing the DSR evaluation activity beyond suggesting possible methods that could be used for evaluation. This paper extends the notable exception of the existing framework of Pries-Heje et al [11] to address this problem. The paper proposes an extended DSR evaluation framework together with a DSR evaluation design method that can guide DSR researchers in choosing an appropriate strategy for evaluation of the design artifacts and design theories that form the output from DSR. The extended DSR evaluation framework asks the DSR researcher to consider (as input to the choice of the DSR evaluation strategy) contextual factors of goals, conditions, and constraints on the DSR evaluation, e.g. the type and level of desired rigor, the type of artifact, the need to support formative development of the designed artifacts, the properties of the artifact to be evaluated, and the constraints on resources available, such as time, labor, facilities, expertise, and access to research subjects. The framework and method support matching these in the first instance to one or more DSR evaluation strategies, including the choice of ex ante (prior to artifact construction) versus ex post evaluation (after artifact construction) and naturalistic (e.g., field setting) versus artificial evaluation (e.g., laboratory setting). Based on the recommended evaluation strategy(ies), guidance is provided concerning what methodologies might be appropriate within the chosen strategy(ies).","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Baskerville, Richard","Venable, John"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-560754"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Curtin University","Georgia State University"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a comprehensive framework for evaluation in design science research","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-560754","identifier":[{"id":"84861206520","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-4796cbf1-af94-410f-bb77-278578b7c9ed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1AC3F88F97A555C6ECDA299FF7718458"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation","Roskilde University, The Department of Communication, Business and Information Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"curtin university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Curtin University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Richard","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"John","key":"venablepau","last":"Venable","name":"Venable, John","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-29863-9_31","issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"423-438","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"7286"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84861206520"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-4796cbf1-af94-410f-bb77-278578b7c9ed"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"A Comprehensive Framework for Evaluation in Design Science Research","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-560754","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
