ject Management Multiplicity : Current Trends","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-570090","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Design theory lies at the heart of information systems design science research. One concern in this area is the potential to limit the designer’s creativity by over-specifying the meta-design or the design process. This paper explains how design research encapsulates a two-person design team consisting of the design theorist and the artifact instance designer. Design theory embodies a creativity passdown effect in which the creative design thinking is partly executed by the design theorist and the completion of this thinking is deferred to the artifact instance designer. In fact, rather than limiting the instance designer’s creativity, the design theorist may create an opportunity for the instance designer to be creative by passing down a design theory. Further, the artifact instance designer operates within the problem domain defined by design theorist, and engages in design thinking to achieve an innovative design by merging theoretical knowledge with experiential knowledge of a design artifact that is being built. The creativity passdown effect was examined through a case that involved developing a tool for multi-outsourcing decision making. The case provides empirical support for the creativity passdown effect.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pries-Heje, Jan","Lee, Jong Seok","Baskerville, Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-571801"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the creativity passdown effect sharing design thinking processes with design theory","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://csdl.computer.org/dl/proceedings/hicss/2012/4525/00/4525e119.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-571801","identifier":[{"id":"84863260343","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-eb02c0b1-7453-42c5-8613-eb9a91134efb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-836C5E915D248FF05CEE9B08E73B86AF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, User-Driven IT Innovation","Roskilde University, The Department of Communication, Business and Information Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"6dbca1cc-ed5b-479e-be59-0cf0ae86a2a8","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jong Seok","key":"leepau","last":"Lee","name":"Lee, Jong Seok","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Richard","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["10603425","15301605"],"issn_org":["10603425"],"journal":"Proceedings of the Annual Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences","pages":"4119-4127","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Annual Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84863260343"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-eb02c0b1-7453-42c5-8613-eb9a91134efb"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"The Creativity Passdown Effect : Sharing Design Thinking Processes with Design Theory","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-571801","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
