 Multiplicity : Current Trends","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-558254","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Projects are everywhere across different sectors, industries and countries. Project management is no longer a sub-discipline of engineering and other rather technical disciplines but is also used for many other purposes. Even though practice has changed dramatically over the years, the models and methodologies for project management has been fairly static and has therefore received substantial criticism for a lack of relevance to practice. Several scholars have therefore started to think more widely about projects and project management conceptualized as rethinking project management. However this theme has lived a somewhat quiet life in Denmark, which leads to the purpose of this chapter, which is to set the stage for rethinking project management in Denmark. The chapter is based on an empirical study within the Danish project management community and beyond where we discuss this rethinking process. The chapter argues for a rethinking process due to pervasiveness and complexity in the contemporary project environment where rethinking is needed in order to stay competitive. The suggested approach for the rethinking project management is a framing process where body of ideas is established and then to diffuse and translate these ideas into practices by a collective action process.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Svejvig, Per"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-233227"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rethinking project management in denmark","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.statsbiblioteket.dk/au/index.jsp?query=project+management+multiplicity&start=0&keepFilter=false&delimitType=available#/search?recordId=sb_5565173","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-233227","ids":["au-b61b819b-34eb-43cf-a22b-af9ff84c9a29"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6005122ABD8F719E4F76A2722DB4453D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.statsbiblioteket.dk/au/index.jsp?query=project+management+multiplicity&start=0&keepFilter=false&delimitType=available#/search?recordId=sb_5565173","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"svejvigpau","last":"Svejvig","locid":"40558617-c35b-464e-a0f6-7a2940494271","name":"Svejvig, Per","orcid":"0000-0002-8758-4031","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepedh","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788759317129 hf."],"pages":"39-58","place":"Frederiksberg","publisher":"Samfundslitteratur","status":"p","subtitle":"Current trends","title":"Project Management Multiplicity"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b61b819b-34eb-43cf-a22b-af9ff84c9a29"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Rethinking Project Management in Denmark","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-233227","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Technologies enabling digital piracy have expanded the variety of options available to users when deciding how to access a product. As a result, access-mode decisions for film and music are broader than for other goods where the piracy option is not as prevalent. This paper presents a model of access-mode decisions for film and music which integrates elements of previous digital piracy models and expands upon them to reflect the decision’s complexity. We depict the access-mode decision as being influenced by the user’s product desire, price perceptions, perceived risks, internal regulators of behaviour, resources and legal availability. We test the model for film and music using causal data of access-mode decisions collected from students at two Danish universities. Our findings indicate that the economic considerations of price perception and legal availability are the most consistent factors in influencing the access-mode decision across different legal options. The paper concludes with an outline for future research.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Veitch, Rob","Constantiou, Ioanna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-286688"],"event":{"end":"2012-06-13","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2012-06-10","title":"20th European Conference on Information Systems, ECIS 2012","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital piracy","Digital products","User behaviour"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"user decisions in a partly digital world comparing digital piracy to legal alternatives for film and music","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/58892845/Veitch_Constantiou_ECIS_2012.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-286688","identifier":[{"id":"84905717766","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-764ed150-ac3a-4b3d-a2eb-df03f0bc57bb"],"keyword":["Adoption decision","Digital piracy","Digital products","User behaviour"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-786EA5A9156B3BAABF3F71694DB78798"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/58892845/Veitch_Constantiou_ECIS_2012.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of IT Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rob","key":"veitchpau","last":"Veitch","locid":"ab59b61c-a1c4-4690-b4ca-0d3f42becfbc","name":"Veitch, Rob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ioanna","key":"constantioupau","last":"Constantiou","locid":"611c88d8-c378-4a3d-ad46-d926fb318515","name":"Constantiou, Ioanna","orcid":"0000-0002-9761-1208","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepedh","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mike","key":"chiassonpedh","last":"Chiasson","name":"Chiasson, Mike","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonathan","key":"warehampedh","last":"Wareham","name":"Wareham, Jonathan","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Xavier","key":"busquetspedh","last":"Busquets","name":"Busquets, Xavier","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Josep","key":"valorpedh","last":"Valor","name":"Valor, Josep","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sandra","key":"seiberpedh","last":"Seiber","name":"Seiber, Sandra","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788488971548"],"issn":["00000034"],"place":"Atlanta, GA","publisher":"Association for Information Systems. AIS Electronic Library (AISeL)","series":"Proceedings of the European Conference on Information Systems","status":"p","title":"ECIS 2012 Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84905717766"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-764ed150-ac3a-4b3d-a2eb-df03f0bc57bb"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"User Decisions in a (Partly) Digital World : Comparing Digital Piracy to Legal Alternatives for Film and Music","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-286688","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
